ed) by Voice Vote."},"laws":[],"number":"2592","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Transportation and Public Works","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001117","district":6,"fullName":"Rep. Casten, Sean [D-IL-6]","party":"D","state":"IL"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-04-02","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Aviation Medication Transparency Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill directs the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) to compile, publish, and annually update a list of medications that may be safely prescribed to pilots and air traffic controllers for the purposes of issuing a medical certification. The list must be publicly available on the FAA website and distributed to those seeking a license and medical&nbsp;certification. </p><p>Currently, the FAA does not have a list of approved medications. However, the FAA does have lists for Aviation Medical Examiners of <em>Do Not Issue</em> medications and <em>Do Not Fly</em> medications.<em></em></p>","updateDate":"2026-05-05T21:43:39Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Aviation Medication Transparency Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:41:19Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:41:19Z"}
